From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 08:39:28 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Count a pairing file another app put in place

iloader writes the pairing file of a LiveContainer+SideStore into the
built-in SideStore's Documents as ALTPairingFile.mobiledevicepairing,
and Cartouche's setup does the same with the file iloader exports. The
boot sequence reads it (fetchPairingFile tries each name), but
hasPairingFile counted only a file under the protocol SideStore had
recorded itself, and before that returned false whenever isPairingReset
was set, which it is from the first launch until SideStore saves a
pairing file itself. So the onboarding asked for a pairing file it
already had. It now counts any file that fetchPairingFile reads, before
looking at isPairingReset: resetAllPairingFiles deletes every file when
it sets it, so a file found afterwards was put there since.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MzPJorvBGmBB88WUcRVhE7
---
 SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
index f7fec76..1f8736a 100644
--- a/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
+++ b/SideStore/Core/Pairing/PairingFileManager.swift
@@ -58,6 +58,15 @@ final class PairingFileManager: NSObject {
     }
 
     nonisolated func hasPairingFile() -> Bool {
+        // A pairing file another app put in place counts: iloader writes one
+        // for a LiveContainer+SideStore, and Cartouche from its setup. The
+        // boot sequence reads it (fetchPairingFile). isPairingReset cannot
+        // rule it out: it is true from the first launch until SideStore saves
+        // a pairing file itself, and resetAllPairingFiles deletes every file
+        // when it sets it.
+        if fetchPairingFile() != nil {
+            return true
+        }
         guard !UserDefaults.standard.isPairingReset else { return false }
         if let target = preferredProtocol, hasPairingFile(for: target) {
             return true
